--- body ---
## Context

Zotero 10.0.2 moved `SDT_SCHEMA_VERSION` 1.1.0 to 1.2.0 and changed the
outline entry shape (`level` gave way to `source`/`target`). The host validates
the schema *major* only, so no stored pack was invalidated and nothing was
announced. `SDT_PROCESSOR_VERSIONS` moved for pdf and epub but not for
`snapshot`, so snapshot packs are regenerated by no upstream event at all.

Measured on doudou 2026-09-11 (`verification/probes/sdt_schema_census.py`):
13 709 packs, 12 774 at schema 1.1.0 and 935 at 1.2.0, of which 4 735 snapshot
packs will hold the superseded form indefinitely.

The author ruled on 2026-09-11: a version change at any depth obliges a repack
of what changed, two pack forms must not coexist, and the superseded form stays
usable during the transition. R1 already promises convergence to the latest
chain with at most two generations coexisting, so a coexistence that cannot
resolve is a standing breach rather than an open question. The full reasoning,
including why refusing the superseded form and why an upstream-only fix both
fail to discharge R1, is the 2026-09-11 entry in DECISIONS.md.

## Relevant files

- `verification/probes/sdt_schema_census.py` — the population reading; the
  before/after evidence for this ticket comes from here.
- `verification/probes/sdt_read.py` — pins `SUPPORTED_PACK_VERSION`, reports
  the schema string without acting on it.
- `SPEC.md` §C1 link 1 and §5.2.4 — the C1 key now takes the pack and schema
  versions at full depth (amended with the ruling).
- `DECISIONS.md` — the 2026-09-11 ruling and the 2026-09-03 entry it corrects;
  also the 0606 entry whose data-directory rejection constrains the mechanism.

## Actions

1. Extend the C1 link-1 staleness key to the full pack and schema versions, so
   a minor bump is a staleness event for text, chunks and vectors.
2. Produce a replacement pack under our own extractor identity, in our own
   store, for any item whose Zotero pack is at a superseded schema. This is
   0606's ratified shape and is why that ticket blocks this one.
3. Amend 0606's precedence rule: Zotero's pack wins wherever one exists *at
   the current schema*; ours overtakes it where Zotero's is superseded and the
   host will never refresh it.
4. Order the convergence newest-first in R1's class order, unattended.
5. Report the transition through R17: how many items on each form, which form
   is answering, and the date.

## Test

Write the red test first: a fixture holding one pack at schema 1.1.0 and one at
1.2.0 for the same source, asserting that the C1 key differs between them. It
fails today, because the key reads processor version and source hash only.

## Verification

- [ ] The census probe shows one form after a convergence run on a fixture
      population seeded with both.
- [ ] An item whose pack is superseded answers queries continuously across the
      whole convergence, measured rather than asserted.
- [ ] Nothing writes to `storage/<KEY>/.zotero-sdt-cache` or anywhere else in
      Zotero's data directory.

## Invariants

- **Never out of service.** The replacement is written before the superseded
  pack stops being used; no window in which the item answers nothing. A clear
  then re-extract sequence violates R4 for the length of the extraction, which
  is minutes per document on the SDT path.
- **Never empties the index.** Refusing the superseded form and booking the
  loss as coverage is excluded by R1 and by the promise the project makes:
  complete *and* current, not current at the price of complete.
- Zotero's data directory stays read-only to us (0606, 2026-09-03).
- At most two generations coexist, and only while converging.

## Exit criteria

The population converges to one form unattended after a version bump at any
depth, the superseded form answers throughout, R17 reports where the transition
has reached, and `make check` passes.

## Upstream arm — needs the author

The defect's real home is upstream: a major-only validity check is what permits
two forms to coexist in one cache at all. Filing that with Zotero is an outward
action and waits for the author's go-ahead. It does not substitute for the work
above, which must converge 4 735 snapshot packs no upstream change would reach.
